{
  "rationale": "The model separates sensing from motion capability and uses small deterministic specifications to bind each sensed condition to exactly one safe action. Clear conditions strongly favor forward progress via move_forward and occasional random_walk, while obstacle conditions force one-shot recovery states: front obstacles trigger a brief backward escape, left obstacles trigger clockwise turning, and right obstacles trigger counterclockwise turning. A small alternation specification prevents endless straight pulses by requiring a brief random_walk after a bounded forward streak, then immediately returning to forward exploration when clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use one sensor plant for uncontrollable obstacle observations and one motion plant for controllable motion primitives.",
    "Use perception-to-action specifications with one-shot commit behavior so obstacle recovery is conservative but brief, and clear states return quickly to forward exploration.",
    "Bias coverage by allowing repeated move_forward in clear space, but insert occasional random_walk through a small forward-streak limiter.",
    "Keep full_rotate available only as a plant capability and do not enable it in the nominal specifications, since it is a last resort not needed for the conservative exploration profile."
  ],
